#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:5
msgid "SwiftUI Mockup Renderer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:7
msgid ""
"Generates native SwiftUI source, compiles it with `swiftc`, renders "
"headlessly via `ImageRenderer`, and captures PNG screenshots in both "
"light and dark mode. The output is pixel-accurate platform UI — real "
"system controls, SF Pro typography, correct spacing, vibrancy, and blur."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:9
msgid "Return contract (read first)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"When this skill runs inside a subagent (the usual case via `ui-designer` "
"or `/mock`), the subagent's narrative return text is **not shown directly"
" to the user** — the orchestrator surfaces a parseable file list. The "
"last thing the subagent emits MUST be a `<MOCKUP_FILES>` block listing "
"every file written:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:13
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<MOCKUP_FILES>\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot.png|Screenshot — light|image\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/screenshot-dark.png|Screenshot — dark|image\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/MockView.swift|SwiftUI source|source\n"
".hero/mocks/{slug}/index.html|Viewer page|primary\n"
".hero/planning/features/{slug}/spec.md|Spec (Mockups section "
"updated)|spec\n"
"</MOCKUP_FILES>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:23
msgid ""
"One file per line, pipe-separated `path|label|kind`. Include both light "
"and dark PNGs even if only one was requested. Skip this block and the "
"user sees no links. See the `ui-designer` agent definition for full "
"rules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:25
msgid "When to use"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:27
msgid ""
"Selection is now driven by `hero spec mock detect` (see `hero spec mock "
"detect --help`). The agent does not decide — the CLI does. This skill is "
"loaded whenever the detect output's `renderer` field is `\"swiftui\"`. "
"Selection drivers (any of):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:29
msgid ""
"Swift stack signals (`.swift`, `Package.swift`, `*.xcodeproj`, "
"`*.xcworkspace`) anywhere `hero spec mock detect` walks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:30
msgid "Explicit `--renderer=swiftui`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:31
msgid "`hero.json` `mockups.renderer: \"swiftui\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:33
msgid ""
"**Prerequisites:** macOS with Xcode command-line tools installed "
"(`swiftc` available on PATH). The CLI gates on this and falls back to "
"HTML (with explicit announce) when `swiftc` is missing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:35
msgid "Source Generation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:37
msgid ""
"Generate a single `MockView.swift` containing all the UI. The file must "
"be self-contained — no package dependencies, no custom assets, no "
"external frameworks beyond SwiftUI and AppKit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:39
msgid "File Structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:41
msgid ""
"// Hero Mock: {slug} | Generated: {date}\n"
"// Description: {one-line description}\n"
"\n"
"import SwiftUI\n"
"import AppKit\n"
"\n"
"// MARK: - Mock View\n"
"\n"
"struct MockView: View {\n"
"    // @State properties for interactivity\n"
"\n"
"    var body: some View {\n"
"        // View hierarchy\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"// MARK: - Supporting Views (if needed)\n"
"\n"
"// Break complex UIs into smaller structs for readability\n"
"\n"
"// MARK: - Capture Entry Point\n"
"\n"
"@main\n"
"struct MockApp {\n"
"    static func main() {\n"
"        let args = CommandLine.arguments\n"
"        let isDark = args.contains(\"--dark\")\n"
"        let width: CGFloat = 390\n"
"        let height: CGFloat = 844\n"
"\n"
"        // Parse --size if provided\n"
"        // Parse --scale if provided (default 2)\n"
"\n"
"        let view = MockView()\n"
"            .frame(width: width, height: height)\n"
"            .environment(\\.colorScheme, isDark ? .dark : .light)\n"
"\n"
"        let renderer = ImageRenderer(content: view)\n"
"        renderer.scale = 2.0\n"
"\n"
"        guard let image = renderer.nsImage else {\n"
"            fputs(\"error: failed to render view\\n\", stderr)\n"
"            exit(1)\n"
"        }\n"
"\n"
"        guard let tiff = image.tiffRepresentation,\n"
"              let bitmap = NSBitmapImageRep(data: tiff),\n"
"              let png = bitmap.representation(using: .png, properties: "
"[:]) else {\n"
"            fputs(\"error: failed to encode PNG\\n\", stderr)\n"
"            exit(1)\n"
"        }\n"
"\n"
"        let outputPath = isDark ? \"screenshot-dark.png\" : "
"\"screenshot.png\"\n"
"        do {\n"
"            try png.write(to: URL(fileURLWithPath: outputPath))\n"
"        } catch {\n"
"            fputs(\"error: \\(error.localizedDescription)\\n\", stderr)\n"
"            exit(1)\n"
"        }\n"
"    }\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:105
msgid ""
"The `@main` entry point is bundled into the same file. This lets `swiftc`"
" compile and run it as a single unit with no project file."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:107
msgid "Design Guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:109
msgid "**Use real SwiftUI components:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:110
msgid "`NavigationStack` / `NavigationSplitView` for navigation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:111
msgid "`List`, `Form`, `Section` for scrollable content"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:112
msgid "`Toggle`, `Picker`, `Slider`, `Stepper` for controls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:113
msgid "`Button`, `Menu`, `Link` for actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:114
msgid "`TabView` for tab-based layouts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:115
msgid "`TextField`, `TextEditor`, `SecureField` for input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:116
msgid "`ProgressView`, `Gauge` for progress"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:117
msgid "`Label`, `LabeledContent` for labeled items"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:118
msgid "`GroupBox`, `DisclosureGroup` for grouping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:120
msgid "**Icons — use SF Symbols:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:121
msgid ""
"Image(systemName: \"gear\")\n"
"Image(systemName: \"person.circle.fill\")\n"
"Image(systemName: \"chart.bar.fill\")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:127
msgid "Never reference custom image assets. SF Symbols are always available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:129
msgid "**Colors — use system semantic colors:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:130
msgid ""
"Color.primary          // adapts to light/dark\n"
"Color.secondary\n"
"Color.accentColor\n"
"Color(.systemBackground)\n"
"Color(.secondarySystemBackground)\n"
"Color(.tertiarySystemBackground)\n"
"Color(.separator)\n"
"Color(.label)\n"
"Color(.secondaryLabel)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:142
msgid "For brand colors, define them inline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:143
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"extension Color {\n"
"    static let heroPrimary = Color(red: 0.29, green: 0.62, blue: 1.0)\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:149
msgid "**Typography — use system styles:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:150
msgid ""
".font(.largeTitle)\n"
".font(.title)\n"
".font(.title2)\n"
".font(.headline)\n"
".font(.subheadline)\n"
".font(.body)\n"
".font(.callout)\n"
".font(.caption)\n"
".font(.footnote)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"**Spacing — use system defaults:** Let SwiftUI handle spacing wherever "
"possible. Use explicit padding only when needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:164
msgid ""
".padding()              // system default (16pt)\n"
".padding(.horizontal)\n"
".padding(8)\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:170
msgid "Layout Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:172
msgid "**Settings / Form screen:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:173
msgid ""
"Form {\n"
"    Section(\"Account\") {\n"
"        LabeledContent(\"Name\", value: \"Sarah Chen\")\n"
