#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:234
msgid "Realistic Data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:236
msgid "Same rules as HTML mockups — use realistic-looking placeholder data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:237
msgid "Names: \"Sarah Chen\", \"Marcus Johnson\", \"Aisha Patel\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:238
msgid "Emails: \"sarah.chen@example.com\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:239
msgid "Dates: relative where possible (`Date.now.addingTimeInterval(-3600)`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:240
msgid "Numbers: realistic ranges (\"$12,847\" not \"$10,000\")"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:241
msgid "Status values: use actual statuses from the spec if available"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:243
msgid "What NOT to Do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:245
msgid "Don't import external packages (no SPM dependencies)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:246
msgid "Don't reference custom image assets or asset catalogs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:247
msgid "Don't use UIKit types (this renders via AppKit on macOS)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:248
msgid ""
"Don't use `@Observable` macro (requires Swift 5.9 macro support — use "
"`@State` instead)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:249
msgid "Don't create Xcode projects or Package.swift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:250
msgid "Don't use `PreviewProvider` — the capture entry point replaces previews"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:251
msgid "Don't add complex animations — they don't render in `ImageRenderer`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:252
msgid "Don't target iOS-only APIs — the code runs on macOS for capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:253
msgid "Don't include more than 2-3 screens in one file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:255
msgid "macOS Compatibility Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:257
msgid ""
"The mockup renders on macOS via `ImageRenderer` + AppKit, even when "
"mocking an iOS app. Key adaptations:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:259
msgid "Use `NavigationStack` (not `NavigationView` deprecated path)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:260
msgid "Avoid `UIScreen`, `UIDevice`, or any UIKit references"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:261
msgid "`ImageRenderer` is available on macOS 13+ / Swift 5.7+"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:262
msgid ""
"The `.frame(width: 390, height: 844)` constrains the render to iPhone "
"dimensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:263
msgid ""
"System controls will render in macOS style — this is acceptable for "
"mockup purposes. The layout, spacing, and content are what matter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:265
msgid "Build and Capture Pipeline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:267
msgid "After generating `MockView.swift`, execute this pipeline:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:269
msgid "Step 1: Verify toolchain"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:270
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"which swiftc || { echo \"swiftc not found — falling back to HTML\"; exit "
"1; }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:274
msgid "Step 2: Compile"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:275
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"cd .hero/mocks/{slug}\n"
"swiftc MockView.swift -framework SwiftUI -framework AppKit -o MockApp "
"2>&1\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:280
msgid ""
"If compilation fails, read the error, attempt one auto-fix of the Swift "
"source, and retry. If the retry also fails, fall back to HTML."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:282
msgid "Step 3: Capture light mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:283
msgid "./MockApp\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:286
msgid "Produces `screenshot.png` in the current directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:288
msgid "Step 4: Capture dark mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:289
msgid "./MockApp --dark\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:292
msgid "Produces `screenshot-dark.png`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:294
msgid "Step 5: Clean up binary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:295
msgid "rm -f MockApp\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:299
msgid "Step 6: Generate viewer HTML"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:301
msgid ""
"Create an `index.html` that displays both screenshots with a light/dark "
"toggle and a collapsible source view. This ensures `hero spec mock "
"--open` and `hero spec mock --serve` keep working."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:303
msgid ""
"**The viewer MUST be a single self-contained file.** Do not reference the"
" PNGs by relative path (`<img src=\"screenshot.png\">`) — a relative path"
" only resolves when the file is served with its own directory as the web "
"root (`--open` / `--serve`), and breaks in embedded preview panes that "
"load the HTML detached from its siblings (via `srcdoc`, a blob URL, or a "
"different web root). Embed both PNGs as base64 `data:image/png;base64,…` "
"URIs so there is no path to resolve. This mirrors the `html-mockup-"
"generation` rule: no external resources, ever."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:305
msgid "First, base64-encode both screenshots:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:306
msgid ""
"LIGHT_B64=$(base64 < screenshot.png | tr -d '\\n')\n"
"DARK_B64=$(base64 < screenshot-dark.png | tr -d '\\n')\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:310
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Then substitute the values into the template's "
"`data:image/png;base64,{LIGHT_B64}` / `{DARK_B64}` slots. (If "
"`swiftui.capture_dark_mode` is off, embed only the light image and drop "
"the toggle.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/swiftui-mockup-renderer/SKILL.md:312
msgid ""
"<!DOCTYPE html>\n"
"<!-- Hero Mock: {slug} | Generated: {date} | Renderer: swiftui -->\n"
"<html lang=\"en\">\n"
"<head>\n"
"    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n"
"    <title>{Title} — Native Mock</title>\n"
"    <style>\n"
"        body { font-family: -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif; margin:"
" 0; padding: 32px; background: #f5f5f5; color: #333; }\n"
"        .header { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-"
"items: center; margin-bottom: 24px; }\n"
"        h1 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; margin: 0; }\n"
"        .badge { background: #d4edda; color: #155724; padding: 2px 10px; "
"border-radius: 12px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }\n"
"        .toggle-bar { display: flex; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 24px; }\n"
"        .toggle-btn { padding: 6px 16px; border: 1px solid #ddd; border-"
"radius: 6px; background: #fff; cursor: pointer; font-size: 13px; }\n"
"        .toggle-btn.active { background: #333; color: #fff; border-color:"
" #333; }\n"
"        .screenshot-frame { background: #fff; border-radius: 12px; box-"
"shadow: 0 2px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.1); display: inline-block; padding: 16px;"
" }\n"
"        .screenshot-frame img { max-width: 100%; height: auto; border-"
"radius: 8px; }\n"
"        .source-toggle { margin-top: 32px; cursor: pointer; font-size: "
"14px; color: #666; }\n"
"        .source-block { display: none; margin-top: 12px; background: "
"#1e1e1e; color: #d4d4d4; padding: 16px; border-radius: 8px; overflow-x: "
"auto; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }\n"
"        .source-block pre { margin: 0; white-space: pre; }\n"
"    </style>\n"
"</head>\n"
"<body>\n"
"    <div class=\"header\">\n"
"        <h1>{Title}</h1>\n"
"        <span class=\"badge\">SwiftUI</span>\n"
"    </div>\n"
"    <div class=\"toggle-bar\">\n"
"        <button class=\"toggle-btn active\" "
"onclick=\"showMode('light')\">Light</button>\n"
"        <button class=\"toggle-btn\" "
"onclick=\"showMode('dark')\">Dark</button>\n"
"    </div>\n"
"    <div class=\"screenshot-frame\">\n"
"        <img id=\"screenshot\"\n"
"             src=\"data:image/png;base64,{LIGHT_B64}\"\n"
"             data-light=\"data:image/png;base64,{LIGHT_B64}\"\n"
"             data-dark=\"data:image/png;base64,{DARK_B64}\"\n"
"             alt=\"Mock screenshot\">\n"
"    </div>\n"
"    <div class=\"source-toggle\" onclick=\"toggleSource()\">&#9654; View "
"SwiftUI source</div>\n"
"    <div class=\"source-block\" id=\"source\">\n"
"        <pre><code>/* Source loaded from MockView.swift */</code></pre>\n"
"    </div>\n"
"    <script>\n"
"        function showMode(mode) {\n"
"            const img = document.getElementById('screenshot');\n"
"            img.src = mode === 'dark' ? img.dataset.dark : "
"img.dataset.light;\n"
"            document.querySelectorAll('.toggle-btn').forEach(b => "
"b.classList.remove('active'));\n"
"            event.target.classList.add('active');\n"
"        }\n"
"        function toggleSource() {\n"
"            const el = document.getElementById('source');\n"
"            const toggle = document.querySelector('.source-toggle');\n"
"            if (el.style.display === 'block') {\n"
"                el.style.display = 'none';\n"
"                toggle.innerHTML = '&#9654; View SwiftUI source';\n"
"            } else {\n"
"                el.style.display = 'block';\n"
"                toggle.innerHTML = '&#9660; Hide SwiftUI source';\n"
"            }\n"
"        }\n"
"    </script>\n"
"</body>\n"
"</html>\n"
msgstr ""

